  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will further strengthen the existing IOM voluntary return mechanism in Japan through continued facilitation of safe and humane return home for irregular migrants. Within the objective of contributing to improving the protection and sustainable reintegration of migrants and migration management of the Government of Japan by providing assisted voluntary return and reintegration services as alternative to long-term detention or forcible removal/deportation, the project&apos;s target outcomes are; migrants with irregular status in Japan who wish to return are able to do so safely, voluntarily and with dignity, and beneficiaries are economically self-sufficient, psychosocially well, and socially integrated in their communities through IOM reintegration assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
